{"id": "sevt_01PZVAtoUUcaaGvaEkNTnctd", "content": [{"text": "Confirmed. Here's the triage.\n\n**Evidence**\n- **Deploys (6h):** checkout `346f34d` 14:41, **cart `df06e76` 14:43:20**, auth `e8f9711` 14:44:50. Only the cart deploy is for the paged service.\n- **Metric alignment:** cart `p99_latency_ms` holds ~75 ms through 14:42, then jumps to **3730 ms at 14:43** and stays ~4000 ms. Deploy 14:43:20 \u2192 p99 moves 14:43. Error rate stays ~0 (slow, not failing).\n- **Diff `df06e76`** (\"price cart lines individually\"): replaced the single batched lookup `SkuPrice.objects.filter(sku_id__in=ids)` + in-memory grouping with a `for line in rows:` loop that runs `SkuPrice.objects.filter(sku_id=line.sku_id)` once per cart line. Classic N+1.\n- **Log confirmation:** per-row `sku_prices WHERE sku_id = ?` queries first appear at **14:43:22** (2s after deploy) and run **~16 per request**; the old batched `WHERE sku_id IN (?)` form dominated before that. Fan-out from 1 query/request to N matches the latency jump.\n\n> **Root cause:** `df06e76` \u2014 refactor replaced the batched `sku_id__in` price lookup with a per-cart-line query (N+1), so cart `price_cart` latency scales with line count and p99 jumped ~75 ms \u2192 ~4000 ms at 14:43.\n\nFix: revert to the batched `sku_id__in` query (or re-group in memory). Roll back `df06e76`.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:30:58.937996Z", "type": "agent.message"}
